I walk over to the counter with my new clothes.
The shop assistant smiles kindly at me.
"Is that everything?" she asks.
"Yes, that is everything," I answer.
She scans all my new things.
There is a sweater, a jacket, a scarf and gloves.
"Now you will not freeze," she says happily.
"That will be one thousand five hundred kroner, please."
The clothes are expensive, but they are very warm.
I take out my payment card.
"I am paying by card," I say.
"You can just pay here," she says.
She points at a small, black machine.
I hold my card over the machine.
It beeps, and the payment is approved.
"Do you want the receipt?" the shop assistant asks.
"No thank you," I answer.
Now I own a lot of nice winter clothes.
